Q("The recruitment pipeline's six stages are:", ["Advert, CV, chat, offer, join, file", "Staffing Plan, Job Opening, Job Applicant, Interview, Job Offer, Employee + Employee Onboarding", "Plan, budget, hire, pay, review, exit", "Opening, offer, employee only"], 1, "Each stage produces a record.", "Ch1"),
Q("The pipeline produces, over informal hiring:", ["Speed only", "Traceability, control (approval before advertising), and reporting from the records", "More paperwork only", "Nothing different"], 1, "Chapter 1's three products.", "Ch1"),
Q("The Staffing Details table row carries:", ["Names of candidates", "Designation, number of positions, current count, and estimated cost per position", "Interview dates", "Offer terms"], 1, "One row per designation planned.", "Ch2"),
Q("The Staffing Plan controls:", ["Interview scheduling", "Job Opening creation — openings validate against the planned positions for the period", "Salary slips", "Leave"], 1, "Vacancies approved before advertised.", "Ch2"),
Q("A blocked but genuinely needed opening is handled by:", ["A bypass", "A plan amendment through its approval", "Ignoring the plan", "A free-text note"], 1, "The control is the approval, not the block.", "Ch2"),
Q("The plan's period close reads:", ["Nothing", "Positions filled within period, positions lapsed, cost against estimate — feeding the next plan", "Applicant counts", "Interview scores"], 1, "The plan-versus-actual discipline.", "Ch2"),
Q("A filled position left with an Open opening:", ["Is harmless", "Overstates the vacancy report — closing is a deliberate act with the hire noted", "Closes itself", "Blocks payroll"], 1, "The status discipline.", "Ch3"),
Q("The Job Opening's Designation link connects it to:", ["The payslip", "The Staffing Plan validation and the downstream applicant and offer records", "The org chart", "The holiday list"], 1, "The canonical title stays on the Designation.", "Ch3"),
